==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Shibalien]]s (1,000%) spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*2 [[Imperator Sael]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Scissoroo]] spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*3 [[Zoge]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Shibalien]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Zigge]]s spawn, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**5 [[Znache]]s spawn, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
**2 [[I.M. Phace]]s spawn, delay 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
**2 [[Scissoroo]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
All [[anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] are required for this stage, otherwise the [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] will be too overwhelming.

With the advent of [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]'s [[Talents]], this stage actually becomes farmable, although the speed is very dependant on Bahamut's level.

==='''Strategy 1 (30s)'''===
{{Lineup
|?
|?
|?
|?
|?
|Jelly Dumpling Cat
|Fishman Cat
|Bullet Train Cat
|Green Shell Cat
|Awakened Bahamut Cat|50
|notes = Fill the top row with as many Starting Money and damage combos as you can. The ideal combination would be a Medium Starting Money, Richest Cat, and the Brave Cutter combo.
}}

Immediately send Jelly Dumpling, then after a little bit use Bullet Train Cat to snipe the Shibalien, then send a Green Shell after that. Dumpling should hit the base and Shell should hit the Scissoroo soon after. Once this happens, spawn everything on the bottom row and wait until you've got enough cash for Bahamut, then send him out. Wait a few more seconds and you win.

==='''Strategy 2 (40/50s)'''===
{{Lineup
|?
|?
|?
|?
|?
|?
|?
|?
|Bullet Train Cat|40
|Awakened Bahamut Cat|40
|notes = Fill the top row with as many damage combos as you can. At least 2 damage combos are needed.
}}

Send out Bullet Train to snipe the initial Shibalien, then send out Awakened Bahamut when you have enough cash. If done correctly, Bahamut should solo the entire base.

